# The left stick as eight sectors -- does a diagonal walk and strafe at once?
#
# The game's own map thresholds each axis at 100 of 127 independently, so a
# push 30 degrees off straight did nothing and no diagonal ever registered.
# In `dual` the left stick is mapped by direction: each of forward, back,
# left and right spans 135 degrees, so a diagonal asks for two. This holds
# the stick at 120 of travel in seven directions and measures the camera's
# own motion per frame (z is a walk, x a strafe) with the yaw held at zero.
#
#   scripts/09-replay.sh --decode --env PSPRECOMP_INPUT=dual \
#     --env PSPRECOMP_VIEW_LOG=reports/sectors.view \
#     --env PSPRECOMP_VIEW_LOG_WORLD=all \
#     --env PSPRECOMP_VIEW_LOG_POLLS=2130-2135,2210-2215,2290-2295,2370-2375,2450-2455,2530-2535,2610-2615 \
#     scenarios/sectors.pad
#   scripts/view-analyze.py reports/sectors.view --deltas

drain 500

@76     state circle 128 128   # t=3.080s
@78     state none 128 128   # t=3.160s
@176    state circle 128 128   # t=7.458s
@178    state none 128 128   # t=7.553s
@317    state circle 128 128   # t=13.327s
@318    state none 128 128   # t=13.379s
